      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "Your framing is correct; you are aiming to raise the \"floor\" of insulin action to preemptively meet the glucose challenge, which is the core principle of advanced basal modulation. In this highly controlled scenario where the primary pathology is massive postprandial oscillation, a judicious 0.6 unit pre-load can indeed mathematically optimize the insulin-to-carb ratio for a flatter curve. However, this strategy is aggressive and demands a very high degree of accuracy in the patient's insulin sensitivity estimations. If the patient's sensitivity is even slightly higher than anticipated, this \"floor raising\" could quickly turn into an under-bolus situation, leading to unexpected lows.",
      "source": "target",
